Turn this portrait into a museum-quality traditional graphite pencil drawing, created entirely by a skilled human artist on fine textured drawing paper. Preserve the exact facial features, expression, hairstyle, proportions, clothing and composition of the original photo. Use realistic graphite techniques including delicate line work, layered cross-hatching, subtle blending, soft tonal transitions, natural pencil strokes, and visible paper texture. Hair should be individually rendered with thousands of hand-drawn strands, eyes highly expressive with realistic reflections, and skin shaded naturally without looking airbrushed. Keep imperfections that exist in real hand drawings such as slight pressure variations, tiny sketch marks and organic pencil texture. Avoid any AI-generated look, digital painting, over-smoothing, plastic skin, exaggerated sharpness or synthetic textures. The final artwork should look like it took an experienced portrait artist 40–60 hours to complete using graphite pencils (2H to 8B), with elegant realism and authentic craftsmanship.

